# Week 3 : News and Financials Tools

This week, I worked on adding two more data sources to the backend: news
and financial data.

## What I did

- Built the news tool (`internal/tools/news.go`), which fetches the latest
  headlines about a company from Google News.
- Built the financials tool (`internal/tools/financials.go`), which looks
  up a stock ticker and returns its price, market cap, P/E ratio, and
  revenue.
- For financials, set it up to try Yahoo Finance first, and fall back to
  scraping Screener.in for Indian company tickers if Yahoo doesn't have the
  data.
- Added a small backup list of hard-coded data for a couple of well-known
  tickers, just in case both live sources fail at the same time.
- Extended the shared data types to include the extra financial fields
  (market cap, P/E ratio, dividend yield, revenue) that weren't needed
  before this tool existed.
- Wired both new tools into the dispatcher so they can be called the same
  way the search tool already is.
- Tested both tools directly with a few real companies and tickers to
  confirm they return sensible data.

At this stage, all three tools (search, news, financials) work on their
own, but none of them are connected to an AI agent yet — that's still
coming later.
